{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-reeb-bundle","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:reeb-bundle","kind":"definition","title":"Reeb bundle over the exceptional divisor","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-exceptional-divisor","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-vector-field"],"tags":["reeb-bundle","exceptional-divisor","hopf-fibration","blow-up"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ReebBundle","text":"reeb-bundle.md","leanSource":"reeb-bundle.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:reeb-bundle\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, \\varTheta, G, \\mathcal{S})</code> be a QOU. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_p \\cong \\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{C})</code> be the exceptional divisor at a brane point <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>. The <strong>Reeb bundle</strong> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code> is the principal <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U(1)</code>-bundle</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{R}_p = \\bigl(S^3 \\xrightarrow{\\pi_H} \\mathcal{S}_p \\cong S^2, \\xi_q\\bigr),</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_H</code> is the Hopf fibration and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi_q</code> is the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Reeb vector field generating the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U(1)</code> fibre action. Its connection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>-form is the one whose holonomy around a generator of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_1(S^1)</code> is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^{2\\pi i / [2]_q}</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2]_q = q + q^{-1}</code> is the quantum integer.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-bundle.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.11.1","page":"b/def-reeb-bundle","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.ReebBundle","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/reeb-bundle.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
